    "description": "What: weather regions you can drive through (CE-1159), on basic-desert at dusk (19:05 UTC). Global weather is clear (25 km visibility, light cloud). A 'Fog bank' (x 140-360, visibility 300 m, fog up to 40 m) and an 'Overcast' region (x 290-510, 8/8 cloud, 6 km visibility) overlap in the middle. An 'IFV (drive east)' at (60, 300) and a 'Rifleman (walk east)' at (60, 280) wait west of both for the user to possess and move. Judge: (1) west of x 140 the sky is clear dusk and distant things are visible (2) entering the fog bank, visibility closes in towards 300 m (3) in the overlap (x 290-360) fog and overcast blend, and east of it the sky is overcast. Fail: the sky or fog does not change at the region edges. Check: none (no live check)"
